omes, schools, workplaces, and government facilities.","learning_objectives":["Understand the basic principles of fire safety.","Identify the common causes of fire incidents.","Apply effective fire prevention practices.","Recognize the different types of fire extinguishers and their appropriate uses.","Demonstrate the proper PASS technique when operating a fire extinguisher.","Follow the correct emergency response and evacuation procedures during a fire incident."],"estimated_duration_minutes":60,"recommended_audience":null,"thumbnail_path":"training-module-thumbnails\\/5J7rKA7ACj0w5MUNtedpX4WTnWai5jc5vEhf2dXu.png","difficulty":"Intermediate","category":"Fire","related_hazard":"Fire","delivery_method":"in_person","target_audience":["residents","barangay_officials","emergency_responders","community_leaders"],"status":"published","visibility":"all","owner_id":3,"lead_qualified_trainer_id":5,"assigned_qualified_trainer_ids":[5,1],"lead_trainer_id":null,"trainer_availability":null,"available_training_sessions":[{"title":"Fire Safety and Emergency Response - Session 1","date":"2026-07-10","start_time":"13:28","end_time":"14:28","delivery_method":"online","venue":"","online_platform":"google_meet","meeting_link":"https:\\/\\/workspace.google.com\\/products\\/meet\\/?utm_source=google&utm_medium=cpc&utm_campaign=1713702-Workspace-DR-APAC-PH-en-Google-BKWS-BRO-Hybrid-Others&utm_content=c-Hybrid+%7C+BKWS+-+BRO+%7C+Txt-Meet-N\\/A+1-297900019805&utm_term=google%20meet&gclsrc=aw.ds&gad_source=1&gad_campaignid=18195926841&gclid=CjwKCAjw6rfSBhAqEiwA_yocpowGRU-kH0T63lHwhYliKozeMpjXCnZooY_sSJqjQQH1PH9aDKP9MRoCdkUQAvD_BwE","maximum_participants":30}],"campaign_registration_opens":"2026-06-28T21:40:00.000000Z","campaign_registration_deadline":"2026-07-19T21:40:00.000000Z","campaign_training_completion_deadline":"2026-07-29T21:40:00.000000Z","campaign_expected_participants":20,"campaign_maximum_participants":30,"campaign_registration_enabled":true,"created_at":"2026-06-27T07:11:29.000000Z","updated_at":"2026-07-26T07:52:38.000000Z","deleted_at":null,"thumbnail_url":"\\/storage\\/training-module-thumbnails\\/5J7rKA7ACj0w5MUNtedpX4WTnWai5jc5vEhf2dXu.png"}', NULL, '2026-07-26 07:52:38', '2026-07-26 07:52:38', '2026-07-26 07:52:38'),
	(261, 3, 'Reymon', 'LGU_ADMIN', 'Published simulation event', 'Simulation Events', 'success', '127.0.0.1', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/150.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', 'http://127.0.0.1:8000/admin/simulation-events/5/publish', 'Title: how use fire extinguisher Original', NULL, '{"id":5,"title":"how use fire extinguisher Original","disaster_type":"Fire Safety","description":"A simulated small electrical fire occurs in the barangay hall\'s common area during a community meeting. Participants must identify the fire type, retrieve the correct fire extinguisher, and apply the PASS method to suppress the fire safely and effectively, while ensuring the safety of others.","event_category":"Functional Exercise","status":"draft","event_date":"2026-07-12T16:00:00.000000Z","start_time":"13:52:00","end_time":"15:00:00","is_recurring":false,"recurrence_pattern":null,"location":"Bestlink","venue":"Bestlink","building":null,"room_zone":null,"location_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"exits":null,"hazard_zones":null,"assembly_points":null,"is_high_risk_location":false,"scenario_id":null,"training_module_id":5,"campaign_request_id":5,"simulation_exercise_template_id":13,"barangay_profile_id":null,"scenario_is_required":true,"facilitators":null,"assigned_trainer_id":5,"allowed_participant_types":null,"target_audience":"Barangay Officials, Community Volunteers","max_participants":25,"registration_deadline":"2026-07-11T05:40:47.000000Z","self_registration_enabled":true,"approval_required":false,"qr_code_enabled":false,"attendance_code":null,"reserved_resources":null,"safety_guidelines":"Always prioritize personal safety; follow all instructions from trainers and safety officers; do not attempt to extinguish large or uncontrolled fires; know the nearest exit routes; report any discomfort or injury immediately to the Medical Team.","hazard_warnings":null,"required_ppe":null,"event_phases":[{"order":1,"title":"Orientation, Registration, and Safety Briefing","duration_minutes":15,"description":"Welcome participants, provide an overview of the exercise objectives and schedule, and conduct a comprehensive safety briefing covering emergency procedures and ground rules for the simulation."},{"order":2,"title":"Lecture-Demonstration: Fire Safety Basics and PASS Method","duration_minutes":30,"description":"A theoretical session covering common causes of fires, types of fire extinguishers (Class A, B, C, D, K), and a detailed demonstration of the \'PASS\' (Pull, Aim, Squeeze, Sweep) method for operating a fire extinguisher."},{"order":3,"title":"Hands-on Practice: Fire Extinguisher Operation","duration_minutes":40,"description":"Participants will individually practice the \'PASS\' method using training fire extinguishers on a controlled, simulated fire (e.g., a fire pan with controlled fuel or a water-based fire simulator). Emphasis on proper stance and technique."},{"order":4,"title":"Scenario Simulation: Responding to a Small Fire Incident","duration_minutes":25,"description":"A controlled functional exercise where participants respond to a simulated small electrical fire in a designated area. Participants will assess the situation, decide on appropriate action, and apply the fire extinguisher as practiced."},{"order":5,"title":"Debriefing and Open Forum","duration_minutes":8,"description":"A facilitated discussion to review the exercise, gather feedback from participants, discuss lessons learned, identify strengths and areas for improvement in fire response."},{"order":6,"title":"Wrap-up and Closing Remarks","duration_minutes":2,"description":"Summary of key takeaways, acknowledgment of participants and personnel, and final announcements."}],"inject_triggers":null,"facilitator_instructions":"Exercise Template: how use fire extinguisher Original\\n\\nRecommended Personnel: Lead Trainer (1), Assistant Trainer (1), Safety Officer (1), Marshal (2), Medical Team (2), Evaluator (1), Communication Officer (1) | Assigned: Lead Trainer: Reymon\\n\\nRecommended Equipment: Fire Extinguisher x1, Fire Extinguisher x3, Fire Extinguisher x1, Emergency Light x1, First Aid Kit x1, Emergency Light x1\\n\\nActivities:\\n1. Orientation, Registration, and Safety Briefing (15 min)\\n2. Lecture-Demonstration: Fire Safety Basics and PASS Method (30 min)\\n3. Hands-on Practice: Fire Extinguisher Operation (40 min)\\n4. Scenario Simulation: Responding to a Small Fire Incident (25 min)\\n5. Debriefing and Open Forum (8 min)\\n6. Wrap-up and Closing Remarks (2 min)\\n\\nEvaluation Objectives:\\n? Participants can correctly identify at least 3 common fire causes and distinguish between different fire extinguisher classes (A, B, C).\\n? At least 90% of participants can demonstrate the \'PASS\' method correctly and safely during hands-on practice.\\n? Participants can effectively assess a simulated small fire scenario, select the appropriate extinguisher, and apply it within 30 seconds of identifying the \'fire\'.\\n? All participants and personnel adhere to established safety protocols throughout the exercise, with no safety breaches reported.\\n? Exercise personnel demonstrate effective coordination and communication in managing the exercise flow and ensuring participant safety.","email_notifications_enabled":true,"sms_notifications_enabled":false,"notification_schedule":null,"created_by":3,"updated_by":3,"published_at":null,"completed_at":null,"created_at":"2026-07-13T05:51:06.000000Z","updated_at":"2026-07-26T06:33:24.000000Z","actual_start_time":null,"started_by":null,"readiness_confirmations":null,"event_personnel_assignments":[{"role":"Lead Trainer","source_group":"group6_trainers","person_name":"Maria Santos","person_external_id":null,"qualified_trainer_id":1,"bpso_personnel_id":null,"patrol_request_id":null,"notes":null},{"role":"Assistant Trainer","source_group":"group6_trainers","person_name":"Carla Mae Mendoza","person_external_id":null,"qualified_trainer_id":11,"bpso_personnel_id":null,"patrol_request_id":null,"notes":null},{"role":"Safety Officer","source_group":"lgu_staff","person_name":"Nestor Quiambao","person_external_id":"346","qualified_trainer_id":null,"bpso_personnel_id":null,"patrol_request_id":null,"notes":null},{"role":"Medical Team","source_group":"lgu_staff","person_name":"Nurse Angelica Dizon","person_external_id":"347","qualified_trainer_id":null,"bpso_personnel_id":null,"patrol_request_id":null,"notes":null},{"role":"Medical Team","source_group":"lgu_staff","person_name":"Dra. Patricia Lim","person_external_id":"342","qualified_trainer_id":null,"bpso_personnel_id":null,"patrol_request_id":null,"notes":null},{"role":"Evaluator","source_group":"lgu_staff","person_name":"Atty. Sofia Manalo","person_external_id":"348","qualified_trainer_id":null,"bpso_personnel_id":null,"patrol_request_id":null,"notes":null},{"role":"Communication Officer","source_group":"lgu_staff","person_name":"Lia Camille Torres","person_external_id":"350","qualified_trainer_id":null,"bpso_personnel_id":null,"patrol_request_id":null,"notes":null}],"execution_progress":null,"timeline_entries":[{"time":"08:15","label":"Orientation, Registration, and Safety Briefing","description":"Welcome participants, provide an overview of the exercise objectives and schedule, and conduct a comprehensive safety briefing covering emergency procedures and ground rules for the simulation."},{"time":"08:30","label":"Lecture-Demonstration: Fire Safety Basics and PASS Method","description":"A theoretical session covering common causes of fires, types of fire extinguishers (Class A, B, C, D, K), and a detailed demonstration of the \'PASS\' (Pull, Aim, Squeeze, Sweep) method for operating a fire extinguisher."},{"time":"09:00","label":"Hands-on Practice: Fire Extinguisher Operation","description":"Participants will individually practice the \'PASS\' method using training fire extinguishers on a controlled, simulated fire (e.g., a fire pan with controlled fuel or a water-based fire simulator). Emphasis on proper stance and technique."},{"time":"09:40","label":"Scenario Simulation: Responding to a Small Fire Incident","description":"A controlled functional exercise where participants respond to a simulated small electrical fire in a designated area. Participants will assess the situation, decide on appropriate action, and apply the fire extinguisher as practiced."},{"time":"10:05","label":"Debriefing and Open Forum","description":"A facilitated discussion to review the exercise, gather feedback from participants, discuss lessons learned, identify strengths and areas for improvement in fire response."},{"time":"10:13","label":"Wrap-up and Closing Remarks","description":"Summary of key takeaways, acknowledgment of participants and personnel, and final announcements."}],"post_evaluation":null}', '{"id":5,"title":"how use fire extinguisher Original","disaster_type":"Fire Safety","description":"A simulated small electrical fire occurs in the barangay hall\'s common area during a community meeting. Participants must identify the fire type, retrieve the correct fire extinguisher, and apply the PASS method to suppress the fire safely and effectively, while ensuring the safety of others.","event_category":"Functional Exercise","status":"published","event_date":"2026-07-12T16:00:00.000000Z","start_time":"13:52:00","end_time":"15:00:00","is_recurring":false,"recurrence_pattern":null,"location":"Bestlink","venue":"Bestlink","building":null,"room_zone":null,"location_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"exits":null,"hazard_zones":null,"assembly_points":null,"is_high_risk_location":false,"scenario_id":null,"training_module_id":5,"campaign_request_id":5,"simulation_exercise_template_id":13,"barangay_profile_id":null,"scenario_is_required":true,"facilitators":null,"assigned_trainer_id":5,"allowed_participant_types":null,"target_audience":"Barangay Officials, Community Volunteers","max_participants":25,"registration_deadline":"2026-07-11T05:40:47.000000Z","self_registration_enabled":true,"approval_required":false,"qr_code_enabled":false,"attendance_code":null,"reserved_resources":null,"safety_guidelines":"Always prioritize personal safety; follow all instructions from trainers and safety officers; do not attempt to extinguish large or uncontrolled fires; know the nearest exit routes; report any discomfort or injury immediately to the Medical Team.","hazard_warnings":null,"required_ppe":null,"event_phases":[{"order":1,"title":"Orientation, Registration, and Safety Briefing","duration_minutes":15,"description":"Welcome participants, provide an overview of the exercise objectives and schedule, and conduct a comprehensive safety briefing covering emergency procedures and ground rules for the simulation."},{"order":2,"title":"Lecture-Demonstration: Fire Safety Basics and PASS Method","duration_minutes":30,"description":"A theoretical session covering common causes of fires, types of fire extinguishers (Class A, B, C, D, K), and a detailed demonstration of the \'PASS\' (Pull, Aim, Squeeze, Sweep) method for operating a fire extinguisher."},{"order":3,"title":"Hands-on Practice: Fire Extinguisher Operation","duration_minutes":40,"description":"Participants will individually practice the \'PASS\' method using training fire extinguishers on a controlled, simulated fire (e.g., a fire pan with controlled fuel or a water-based fire simulator). Emphasis on proper stance and technique."},{"order":4,"title":"Scenario Simulation: Responding to a Small Fire Incident","duration_minutes":25,"description":"A controlled functional exercise where participants respond to a simulated small electrical fire in a designated area. Participants will assess the situation, decide on appropriate action, and apply the fire extinguisher as practiced."},{"order":5,"title":"Debriefing and Open Forum","duration_minutes":8,"description":"A facilitated discussion to review the exercise, gather feedback from participants, discuss lessons learned, identify strengths and areas for improvement in fire response."},{"order":6,"title":"Wrap-up and Closing Remarks","duration_minutes":2,"description":"Summary of key takeaways, acknowledgment of participants and personnel, and final announcements."}],"inject_triggers":null,"facilitator_instructions":"Exercise Template: how use fire extinguisher Original\\n\\nRecommended Personnel: Lead Trainer (1), Assistant Trainer (1), Safety Officer (1), Marshal (2), Medical Team (2), Evaluator (1), Communication Officer (1) | Assigned: Lead Trainer: Reymon\\n\\nRecommended Equipment: Fire Extinguisher x1, Fire Extinguisher x3, Fire Extinguisher x1, Emergency Light x1, First Aid Kit x1, Emergency Light x1\\n\\nActivities:\\n1. Orientation, Registration, and Safety Briefing (15 min)\\n2. Lecture-Demonstration: Fire Safety Basics and PASS Method (30 min)\\n3. Hands-on Practice: Fire Extinguisher Operation (40 min)\\n4. Scenario Simulation: Responding to a Small Fire Incident (25 min)\\n5. Debriefing and Open Forum (8 min)\\n6. Wrap-up and Closing Remarks (2 min)\\n\\nEvaluation Objectives:\\n? Participants can correctly identify at least 3 common fire causes and distinguish between different fire extinguisher classes (A, B, C).\\n? At least 90% of participants can demonstrate the \'PASS\' method correctly and safely during hands-on practice.\\n? Participants can effectively assess a simulated small fire scenario, select the appropriate extinguisher, and apply it within 30 seconds of identifying the \'fire\'.\\n? All participants and personnel adhere to established safety protocols throughout the exercise, with no safety breaches reported.\\n? Exercise personnel demonstrate effective coordination and communication in managing the exercise flow and ensuring participant safety.","email_notifications_enabled":true,"sms_notifications_enabled":false,"notification_schedule":null,"created_by":3,"updated_by":3,"published_at":"2026-07-26T08:43:49.000000Z","completed_at":null,"created_at":"2026-07-